    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I agree with @Haroenv here. If the behaviour is broken and the user would not be able to use it, it is better to throw an error. Warnings can be easily ignored and the user would spend more time to investigate why he doesn't have the desired behaviour. \r\nWarnings should be use in cases where maybe it is not the recommended way of using or doing something but would still work",
