    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "We've historically never checked in any other widgets if the container isn't a `div` (or any element that acts like a container, e.g. `article`). This is why I figured there's no more reason to keep this check here, except if we do it in _all_ other widgets.\r\n\r\nIf you use the `refinementList` widget in an `input` element, it won't work either, but we don't check this kind of misusage.\r\n\r\n@robertmogos I chose the word \"might\" because there's no guarantee that it works on our side (it depends on the DOM implementation). To be more accurate, it won't work in this case (but again, neither will any other widgets).",
    "commit_id": "f7c21a17a9f8e70aca447a5cb477deb1e0238823",
    "created_at": "2019-01-25T14:29:17Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -217,25 +222,20 @@ export default function searchBox({\n \n   const containerNode = getContainerNode(container);\n \n-  if (containerNode.tagName === 'INPUT') {\n-    // eslint-disable-next-line\n-    // FIXME: the link should be updated when the documentation is migrated in the main Algolia doc\n-    throw new Error(\n-      `[InstantSearch.js] Since in version 3, \\`container\\` can not be an \\`input\\` anymore.\n+  warning(",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/pull/3422#discussion_r251003242",
